---
import QuestionLayout from '@layouts/QuestionLayout.astro';

const jsonLd = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [{
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: 'What is the model.execute catalog capability?',
    acceptedAnswer: {
      '@type': 'Answer',
      text: 'model.execute@1.0.0 is a capability in the Traverse registry catalog (published Oct 15, 2026, registry#639, index-v407) that lets agents and apps find governed model execution through discover → execute → trace. It is a thin shim over the host connector traverse.model-runtime: the caller supplies an exact-ref model pin (model_id, version, digest), a host-staged input_ref, model_usage (commercial or non_commercial), and a trust_root of allowed signer key ids. The capability checks those inputs, dispatches through the mediated connector, and returns the host model_evidence or a fail-closed Spec 138 reason unchanged. It does not fetch models, hold keys, or pick a model. It pins traverse.model-runtime 2.3.0, which is on Traverse main and not in the published v0.15.0 hosts, and its registry spec (027) is still a draft.',
    },
  }],
});

const relatedLinks = [
  { href: '/questions/what-is-exact-ref-model-execution.html', label: 'What is exact-ref model execution?' },
  { href: '/questions/what-is-exact-model-host.html', label: 'What is ExactModelHost?' },
